 "recipe": "span return with inverse-noise loss weighting (Rw)",
 "recipe_description": "the copy-pointer carrier network (61,613 parameters) trained from scratch per population on a pooled training set (windows whose labels end before the population's validation set), early stopping on the population's last 93 days before the training cut (at most 30 epochs, patience 5); then the 93-day validation span returned to the training set at the population's own sampling density (labels ending within 24 h of the cut not returned) and training continued from the selected weights with a fresh AdamW for exactly 8 epochs, final weights kept; the loss of these 8 epochs weighted per training window by the frozen inverse-noise rule (omega = max(sigma^2, floor)^-1/2, sigma^2 from the window's own context day tokens 338..365 against the same hours 7 days earlier, floor = the draw-probability-weighted 25th percentile, weights normalised to a draw-weighted mean of 1 within each source population); seeds 0 to 5 averaged at every issue time, anchored by the unchanged ANKYRA 2.2.1 anchoring layer, weekly seasonal naive on off-state and micro-load windows; then the origin-continuity layer (ankyra_lite.continuation, frozen constants) on the anchored trajectory of the other windows, with energy, level and peak read before the layer (readout rule A)",
 "note": "Paths are relative to the research root (environment variable ANKYRA_LITE_RESEARCH_ROOT, default <repo>/../HKAD_V3). 'npz' is the anchored product before the continuation layer (the 0.1.0 format: building, origin, traj, level, peak, off, micro; plus state and the layer's pre-origin inputs cont_pre672, cont_last_type, cont_day_types); 'continued_npz' the same product with the layer (traj = the delivered trajectory, traj_anchored = the trajectory before the layer, level and peak unchanged, cont_* = the layer's record); 'group_npz' / 'group_continued_npz' the two three-seed groups of a six-seed configuration (seeds 0-2, 3-5), before and after the layer; 'run_dirs' the stage-2 run of every seed (carrier.npz: the carrier forecasts at the origin and the six pseudo-origins and the training cut; COMPLETE.json, TRAINED.json; the weights file named by 'checkpoint'); 'start_run_dirs' the from-scratch stage each run continued (best.pt); 'weights_record' the frozen loss weights of recipe Rw; 'span_plan' the returned validation span; 'prep' temp_sigma_std and the split record; 'recipe_variants' the other configurations and the 0.1.x recipe arms on the same windows. 'store': 'original' = the population's store as first built; 'corrected' = trained with the corrected CINELDI store (for CINELDI its own data, CINELDI origins = original origins + 1,416 h; for Drammen the CINELDI windows of its pooled training set).",
